win32: export GetFileSizeEx and TryAcquireSRWLockExclusive

GetFileSizeEx is declared in fileapi.h and winbase.h, and
TryAcquireSRWLockExclusive is declared in synchapi.h behind the same
_WIN32_WINNT 0x0600 gate as the other SRW lock functions. Neither symbol is
in kernel32.def, so a program that calls either one, or links an object such
as SQLite 3.54.0 that references them, fails with "unresolved reference".

Add both kernel32 exports. The declarations are unchanged, so this patch only
affects linking. Patch 0015 exports the other SRW lock functions.
diff --git a/win32/lib/kernel32.def b/win32/lib/kernel32.def
index f768b601..dd105965 100644
--- a/win32/lib/kernel32.def
+++ b/win32/lib/kernel32.def
@@ -269,6 +269,7 @@ GetFileAttributesExW
 GetFileAttributesW
 GetFileInformationByHandle
 GetFileSize
+GetFileSizeEx
 GetFileTime
 GetFileType
 GetFullPathNameA
@@ -688,6 +689,7 @@ TlsSetValue
 Toolhelp32ReadProcessMemory
 TransactNamedPipe
 TransmitCommChar
+TryAcquireSRWLockExclusive
 TryEnterCriticalSection
 UTRegister
 UTUnRegister
